1. RM command – Remove an unwanted file
cd Desktop


Create a sample file:
touch unwanted.txt


Display the file:
ls


Remove the file:
rm unwanted.txt


Verify deletion:
ls


2. USERS command – Display logged-in users
Execute:
users


Example output:
kali


3. TREE command – Display directory structure
First install tree:
sudo apt update


sudo apt install tree -y


Display the directory structure:
tree


Display hidden files and folders:
tree -a


Display only the first two directory levels:
tree -L 2
